// DGA-owned native menu fields. Limits match readSettings(); no native profile IDs.
{"Dynamic Gameday Attendance",L"Dynamic Gameday Attendance",L"Enabled","Enabled","Enables changing crowds and the sound that follows their attendance. Turning this off does not turn off the separate extra-replay options below.",1.0,0.0,1.0,Kind::Toggle},
{"Dynamic Gameday Attendance",L"Dynamic Gameday Attendance",L"Profile","Departure Profile","Auto follows the matchup and weather. Reduced keeps fans more patient; Bad Weather makes them less patient. This affects departures, not audio qualification.",0,0,3,Kind::Profile},
{"Dynamic Gameday Attendance",L"Dynamic Gameday Attendance",L"ArrivalsEnabled","Arrivals Enabled","Starts with some seats empty and fills toward the game's original crowd in Q1. Turning this off skips late arrivals; it does not force the game to sell out.",1.0,0.0,1.0,Kind::Toggle},
{"Dynamic Gameday Attendance",L"Dynamic Gameday Attendance",L"StartPercent","Start (%)","Normal schools start here before a combined matchup/weather adjustment of -10 to +10 points. Former moderate-late schools now use this group. Range 30-90; default 55.",55.0,30.0,90.0,Kind::Slider},
{"Dynamic Gameday Attendance",L"Dynamic Gameday Attendance",L"LateSchoolStartPercent","Late School Start (%)","UCLA, Miami (FL), Georgia Tech and Maryland start here. Range 30-80; default 40.",40.0,30.0,80.0,Kind::Slider},
{"Dynamic Gameday Attendance",L"Dynamic Gameday Attendance",L"FinishPercentOfQuarter","Finish (%) Of Quarter","Normal schools finish their arrivals this far through Q1. Default 25 = one quarter of Q1.",25.0,10.0,100.0,Kind::Slider},
{"Dynamic Gameday Attendance",L"Dynamic Gameday Attendance",L"LateSchoolFinishPercentOfQuarter","Late School Finish (%) Of Quarter","Severe-late schools finish this far through Q1. Default 75 = three quarters of Q1. These timings scale with quarter length; matchup/weather change the start, not the finish time.",75.0,10.0,100.0,Kind::Slider},
{"Dynamic Gameday Attendance",L"Dynamic Gameday Attendance",L"HalftimeSeatBreakStrength","Halftime Seat Break Strength","100 temporarily removes 20-30% of the fans still present, subject to crowd floors. They leave over the last quarter of Q2 and return over the first quarter of Q3. Changes wait for hidden breaks/play selection. 0 disables; max 200 doubles the share.",100.0,0.0,200.0,Kind::Slider},
{"Dynamic Gameday Attendance",L"Dynamic Gameday Attendance",L"HalftimeDepartureConversionPercent","Halftime Departure Conversion (%)","Some halftime seat-breakers stay gone when an ordinary home game turns ugly. 0 disables it; default/max 25. At an 18-point home deficit the share is about 20%, rising smoothly to 25% at 28+ points. It fades out as fewer than 90% of fans remain, and is off at 80% remaining.",25.0,0.0,25.0,Kind::Slider},
{"Dynamic Gameday Attendance",L"Dynamic Gameday Attendance",L"BigGameBonus","Big Game Bonus","Rivalry starting-crowd bonus, capped at 10 points. Rivalry alone no longer makes a big game.",10.0,0.0,10.0,Kind::Slider},
{"Dynamic Gameday Attendance",L"Dynamic Gameday Attendance",L"BigGameStartPercent","Big Game Start (%)","Both-Top-25 and postseason games share this baseline. Hard minimum 60; range 60-90. Rivalry can add up to 10 and bad weather subtracts up to 10, but never below 60.",60.0,60.0,90.0,Kind::Slider},
{"Dynamic Gameday Attendance",L"Dynamic Gameday Attendance",L"BadWeatherPenalty","Bad Weather Penalty","Rain/snow starting-crowd penalty, 0-10 points.",10.0,0.0,10.0,Kind::Slider},
{"Dynamic Gameday Attendance",L"Dynamic Gameday Attendance",L"FcsOpponentPenalty","Fcs Opponent Penalty","FCS starting-crowd penalty, 0-10. Included within the combined -10/+10 adjustment.",10.0,0.0,10.0,Kind::Slider},
{"Dynamic Gameday Attendance",L"Dynamic Gameday Attendance",L"ComebackOriginalDeficit","Comeback Original Deficit","How far behind the home team must have been before a comeback can buy patience. Example: 21 means it must have trailed by at least three touchdowns. Range: 14-100.",21.0,14.0,100.0,Kind::Slider},
{"Dynamic Gameday Attendance",L"Dynamic Gameday Attendance",L"ComebackPointsRecovered","Comeback Points Recovered","Points made up before that comeback can help keep fans interested. Range: 7-100.",14.0,7.0,100.0,Kind::Slider},
{"Dynamic Gameday Attendance",L"Dynamic Gameday Attendance",L"ComebackDeteriorationSeconds","Comeback Deterioration Seconds","Game-clock seconds of a deteriorating comeback before that protection ends. Based on 12-minute quarters and adjusted for your quarter length. Range: 0-600.",60.0,0.0,600.0,Kind::Slider},
{"Dynamic Gameday Attendance",L"Dynamic Gameday Attendance",L"TwoMinuteWarning","Two Minute Warning","Adds a departure decision at the next safe break after Q4 reaches 2:00.",1.0,0.0,1.0,Kind::Toggle},
{"Dynamic Gameday Attendance",L"Dynamic Gameday Attendance",L"MaximumDeparturePerQuarter","Maximum Departure Per Quarter","Standard permanent-departure limit in one ordinary quarter: 1-50 points of the original crowd. Hopeless late home blowouts can use the limited extra allowance below. Postseason games keep their own lower limits.",45.0,1.0,50.0,Kind::Slider},
{"Dynamic Gameday Attendance",L"Dynamic Gameday Attendance",L"MaximumDeparturePerTransition","Maximum Departure Per Transition","Base size of a visible crowd-change step at a safe break: 1-20 points. Longer waits allow larger steps; halftime returns and arrivals use this too. Built-up permanent departures can catch up faster. Quarter limits still apply.",4.0,1.0,20.0,Kind::Slider},
{"Dynamic Gameday Attendance",L"Dynamic Gameday Attendance",L"LateTrafficEnabled","Late Traffic Enabled","In the last quarter of Q4, fans leave faster when a home comeback looks unlikely. Uses the deficit, time left, possession, timeouts and recent home scoring. With 12-minute quarters, this begins inside the final three minutes. It moves toward one target, not another repeated percentage cut.",1.0,0.0,1.0,Kind::Toggle},
{"Dynamic Gameday Attendance",L"Dynamic Gameday Attendance",L"LateTrafficExtraQuarterAllowance","Late Traffic Extra Quarter Allowance","Extra points allowed beyond the standard Q4 departure cap when the home team trails by 28+ in the final 25% of Q4 (last 3 minutes with 12-minute quarters). Scales with deficit, time remaining and recovery outlook; never refills a crowd.",10.0,0.0,10.0,Kind::Slider},
{"Dynamic Gameday Attendance",L"Dynamic Gameday Attendance",L"LateTurnoverExtraMax","Late Turnover Extra Max","Maximum extra original-crowd points after a costly late home interception/lost fumble: 0-15. Default 10. A smaller chance-changing turnover gets fewer; hopeful games get none. A same-play late score and turnover use the larger group, never both added together.",10.0,0.0,15.0,Kind::Slider},
{"Dynamic Gameday Attendance",L"Dynamic Gameday Attendance",L"FormulaStrength","Formula Strength","How strongly score, clock and matchup encourage permanent departures: 0-200. 100 = normal, 50 = gentler, 200 = stronger, 0 = no formula departures. Temporary seat breaks and the separate late-score rule have their own controls.",100.0,0.0,200.0,Kind::Slider},
{"Dynamic Gameday Attendance",L"Dynamic Gameday Attendance",L"LateScoreExtra","Late Score Extra","Extra original-crowd points who may leave after a late opponent score: 0-25. Applies in Q4's final two minutes when home trails by 9+ with 0-1 timeouts. Postseason and neutral-site games are excluded. Set 0 to disable this rule.",5.0,0.0,25.0,Kind::Slider},
{"Dynamic Gameday Soundscape",L"Dynamic Gameday Soundscape",L"Enabled","Enabled","Enables seating-fullness-based volume and the added crowd audio system. Soundscape waits for a verified seating measurement; attendance percentages are separate. Visual attendance and extra replay frequency remain separate. Enabling after an off-at-launch session needs a game restart.",1.0,0.0,1.0,Kind::Toggle},
{"Dynamic Gameday Soundscape",L"Dynamic Gameday Soundscape",L"NativeQuietingStrengthPercent","Native Quieting Strength (%)","Strength of small-crowd quieting: 0-100. 0 disables it; 100 uses the tested profile. Changes fade over about six seconds. High native excitement receives an extra sparse-crowd peak trim. Below the fullness threshold, venues with up to 10,000 mapped positions settle below 100 excitement.",100.0,0.0,100.0,Kind::Slider},
{"Dynamic Gameday Soundscape",L"Dynamic Gameday Soundscape",L"CrowdVolumeReductionPercent","Crowd Volume Reduction (%)","Gentle crowd-volume cut below ReductionStartPercent fullness, in addition to calmer native voices. Only venues with 12,000 or fewer verified mapped seating positions use this cut. Larger venues use native intensity quieting below 50% fullness, without this volume cut. Default 25; range 0-25.",25.0,0.0,25.0,Kind::Slider},
{"Dynamic Gameday Soundscape",L"Dynamic Gameday Soundscape",L"ReductionStartPercent","Reduction Start (%)","Below this seating fullness, the native crowd bed gradually becomes calmer. Default 50; range 1-50. This changes the crowd's excitement, not a shared volume slider.",50.0,1.0,50.0,Kind::Slider},
{"Dynamic Gameday Soundscape",L"Dynamic Gameday Soundscape",L"LayeredAtmosphereEnabled","Layered Atmosphere","Enables added roar/cheer layers, extra excitement, shake and volume boosts. Visual attendance and the small-crowd quieting controls above remain separate.",1.0,0.0,1.0,Kind::Toggle},
{"Dynamic Gameday Soundscape",L"Dynamic Gameday Soundscape",L"OpeningAtmosphere","Opening Atmosphere","Enables qualified stadium-intro atmosphere and extra early-Q1 play-call energy. Actual big games get opening buildup from 50% measured fullness, including the intro. The normal size-based requirement returns gradually from 10% to 75% through Q1.",1.0,0.0,1.0,Kind::Toggle},
{"Dynamic Gameday Soundscape",L"Dynamic Gameday Soundscape",L"OvertimeAtmosphere","Overtime Atmosphere","Lets eligible overtime keep its layered crowd sound between snaps. Fullness needed scales from 85% at 6,060 positions to 50% at 61,888. Ordinary departure calculations stop in competitive OT.",1.0,0.0,1.0,Kind::Toggle},
{"Dynamic Gameday Soundscape",L"Dynamic Gameday Soundscape",L"PlayCallAtmosphere","Play Call Atmosphere","Enables play-call roar/swell/cheer layers and ordinary successful-play reactions. Eligible calls use roars/swells over 40 seconds. Most calls have no added cheer. Home-offense cheers: inside the 10, first home offensive call, first call of a late winning drive.",1.0,0.0,1.0,Kind::Toggle},
{"Dynamic Gameday Soundscape",L"Dynamic Gameday Soundscape",L"UpsetWatchAtmosphere","Upset Watch Atmosphere","Separate sound route for a home underdog challenging a Top 25 visitor from Q2 onward. Verified ranking gap, score and game stage ease the normal size-based sound gate, never below 50% actual seating fullness. Modest Q2 buildup grows with a credible late bid. Neutral venues follow either underdog.",1.0,0.0,1.0,Kind::Toggle},
{"Dynamic Gameday Soundscape",L"Dynamic Gameday Soundscape",L"SkillMoveReactions","Skill Move Reactions","Adds short cheer/shake accents for confirmed successful trucks, stiff arms, hurdles, jukes, spins, broken tackles and landed hit sticks. Attempts do not count. Uses the existing fullness/layered-atmosphere gates. Touchdowns/eruptions take priority. Default 1; range 0-1. 1 = enabled, 0 = disabled.",1.0,0.0,1.0,Kind::Toggle},
{"Dynamic Gameday Soundscape",L"Dynamic Gameday Soundscape",L"StaggeredMajorCheers","Staggered Major Cheers","Major plays and eruptions may add one second cheer about 0.9 seconds later. Includes the game's own cheers in a two-reaction limit; never loops or raises volume caps. Default 1; range 0-1. 1 = enabled, 0 = no delayed second cheer.",1.0,0.0,1.0,Kind::Toggle},
{"Dynamic Gameday Soundscape",L"Dynamic Gameday Soundscape",L"PackedBigGameReactions","Packed Big Game Reactions","Adds context to reactions only in packed ranked/championship games or packed rivalries. Close late downs and goal-line plays get stronger reactions; confirmed game-sealing stops can erupt and a first down that allows kneeling out the clock gets a scoring-style response.",1.0,0.0,1.0,Kind::Toggle},
{"Dynamic Gameday Soundscape",L"Dynamic Gameday Soundscape",L"DuringPlayReactionsEnabled","During Play Reactions Enabled","Enables the extra long-gain, interception, return and defensive-impact reactions. Added reactions inherit the size-based fullness requirement of their qualifying play. Includes long gains, interceptions, live native forced-fumble events, confirmed sacks and 30-yard returns.",1.0,0.0,1.0,Kind::Toggle},
{"Dynamic Gameday Soundscape",L"Dynamic Gameday Soundscape",L"LongCompletionMinimumYards","Long Completion Minimum Yards","Minimum yards gained at the catch for an immediate long-completion reaction: 10-60. Default 20. Immediately tackled catches receive a short impact and settling fade. Short catches can qualify separately if the receiver turns them into a long gain.",20.0,10.0,60.0,Kind::Slider},
{"Dynamic Gameday Soundscape",L"Dynamic Gameday Soundscape",L"LongGainMinimumYards","Long Gain Minimum Yards","Total gain needed for a run or catch-and-run reaction, measured from the snap: 10-60. The cheer triggers at this distance. Shake builds over the preceding five yards. Default 15: 1% shake at 10 yards, rising to normal live-play strength at 15.",15.0,10.0,60.0,Kind::Slider},
{"Dynamic Gameday Soundscape",L"Dynamic Gameday Soundscape",L"PassFlightAnticipation","Airborne Pass Swells","Adds anticipation while a verified pass is in flight on an eligible layered play. Uses the existing native gameplay swell with a 0.5-second attack, even if a lineup roar is playing. One swell opportunity per pass; settles after catch/incompletion. Requires DuringPlayReactionsEnabled.",1.0,0.0,1.0,Kind::Toggle},
{"Dynamic Gameday Soundscape",L"Dynamic Gameday Soundscape",L"SituationalCrowdReactions","Situational Crowd Reactions","Adds native crowd disappointment to failed home conversions, deep incompletions, home interceptions and deep visitor catches. Deep passes need 15+ air yards. Home defensive deep incompletions/breakups and tackles for loss get a cheer.",1.0,0.0,1.0,Kind::Toggle},
{"Dynamic Gameday Soundscape",L"Dynamic Gameday Soundscape",L"ChantMaximumBoostPercent","Chant Maximum Boost (%)","Maximum chant boost at a completely full stadium: 0-15%. Starts at no boost at 75% fullness, then rises in a straight line to this limit. Chants do not inherit the larger general-crowd or eruption boosts.",15.0,0.0,15.0,Kind::Choice},
{"Dynamic Gameday Soundscape",L"Dynamic Gameday Soundscape",L"BigGameMinimumFullnessPercent","Big Game Fullness Floor (%)","Optional extra floor for big-game buildup: 55-90. Default 55 leaves the size curve intact. Big games, close critical downs and goal-line tension normally need 90% fullness at 6,060 stored positions, scaling to 55% at 61,888. Size endpoints clamp beyond those sizes.",55.0,55.0,90.0,Kind::Slider},
{"Dynamic Gameday Soundscape",L"Dynamic Gameday Soundscape",L"WinningEruptions","Winning Eruptions","Enables special eruptions for qualifying early/long touchdowns, decisive late scores, OT winners/takeaways, late defensive takeaways and major upset wins. Late takeaways need a one-score lead and enough clock to kneel out the game: final 60 seconds with 0-1 opponent timeouts, or final 40 with 2.",1.0,0.0,1.0,Kind::Toggle},
{"Dynamic Gameday Soundscape",L"Dynamic Gameday Soundscape",L"PackedHouseBuildup","Packed House Buildup","Lets ordinary matchups get play-call buildup based on the stadium's stored seating size. Required fullness scales from 98% at 6,060 positions to 60% at 61,888. Smaller venues use 98%; larger venues use 60%. Empty positions count toward size.",1.0,0.0,1.0,Kind::Toggle},
{"Dynamic Gameday Soundscape",L"Dynamic Gameday Soundscape",L"DriveEscalation","Drive Escalation","Successful drives strengthen the existing layers; stalls and game time cool them. This adds excitement, not another volume bonus. Possession changes/scores reset it.",1.0,0.0,1.0,Kind::Toggle},
{"Dynamic Gameday Soundscape",L"Dynamic Gameday Soundscape",L"MaximumBoostPercent","Maximum Crowd Boost (%)","Maximum ordinary general-crowd boost at full seating: 0-25%. No ordinary boost at 75% fullness; rises linearly above that. 0 also disables added sound layers. Use their individual switches for finer control.",25.0,0.0,25.0,Kind::Choice},
{"Dynamic Gameday Soundscape",L"Dynamic Gameday Soundscape",L"HighLeverageBoostPercent","Critical Moment Boost (%)","Total general-crowd boost limit for close third/fourth downs, near-goal scoring threats, overtime and late scoring-drive buildup: 0-35%. Does not stack on 25%. Lower values do not pull a moment below the ordinary fullness-based volume.",35.0,0.0,35.0,Kind::Choice},
{"Dynamic Gameday Soundscape",L"Dynamic Gameday Soundscape",L"EruptionBoostPercent","Eruption Boost (%)","Total general-crowd boost limit for special eruptions: 0-50%. This replaces the ordinary target during the moment; it is not another 50% on top. 0 keeps ordinary volume; use WinningEruptions=0 to turn the eruption itself off.",50.0,0.0,50.0,Kind::Choice},
{"Dynamic Gameday Broadcast",L"Dynamic Gameday Broadcast",L"ExtraReplaysEnabled","Extra Replays Enabled","Enables the mod's extra post-play replay opportunities. Does not turn off the game's existing replays or attendance history in replays.",1.0,0.0,1.0,Kind::Toggle},
{"Dynamic Gameday Broadcast",L"Dynamic Gameday Broadcast",L"PauseMenuFullness","Pause Menu Fullness","Shows Stadium Fullness beside Resume in the regular pause menu. Uses the visible seating measurement that controls crowd sound, not attendance remaining. Refreshes when the menu opens. -- means a reliable seating measurement is not ready.",1.0,0.0,1.0,Kind::Toggle},
{"Dynamic Gameday Broadcast",L"Dynamic Gameday Broadcast",L"InsetAfterRoutinePlays","Inset After Routine Plays","Allows routine runs/completions to use the small replay during play selection.",1.0,0.0,1.0,Kind::Toggle},
{"Dynamic Gameday Broadcast",L"Dynamic Gameday Broadcast",L"FullScreenBigPlays","Full Screen Big Plays","Encourages the game's full-screen big-play sequences; normal skip controls stay.",1.0,0.0,1.0,Kind::Toggle},
{"Dynamic Gameday Broadcast",L"Dynamic Gameday Broadcast",L"DefensiveHighlights","Defensive Highlights","Adds defensive replay opportunities for sacks/TFLs and keeps the native interception/lost-fumble presentation. Does not invent turnovers or change stats.",1.0,0.0,1.0,Kind::Toggle},
{"Dynamic Gameday Broadcast",L"Dynamic Gameday Broadcast",L"FullScreenMinimumYards","Full Screen Minimum Yards","Yardage threshold for those full-screen sequences: 10-60 yards. Native first-down and special-scene requirements can still affect the selection.",15.0,10.0,60.0,Kind::Slider},
{"Dynamic Gameday Broadcast",L"Dynamic Gameday Broadcast",L"CameraShake","Camera Shake","Enables the mod's added camera movement. 0 turns all added types off. Respects the game's camera-effects accessibility setting. Gameplay HFA stays native.",1.0,0.0,1.0,Kind::Toggle},
{"Dynamic Gameday Broadcast",L"Dynamic Gameday Broadcast",L"NativeShakeMinimumFullnessPercent","Native Shake Minimum Fullness (%)","Suppress the game's own Stadium Pulse camera shake below this actual seating fullness. Default 50; range 0-100. 0 disables this filter. Fuller stadiums keep native shake. Camera presentation only: the Pulse meter and gameplay home-field advantage stay unchanged.",50.0,0.0,100.0,Kind::Slider},
{"Dynamic Gameday Broadcast",L"Dynamic Gameday Broadcast",L"OrdinaryShakeStrengthPercent","Ordinary Shake Strength (%)","Camera movement strengths, not sound volume or Stadium Pulse meter levels. All added shake softens on zoomed cameras, including ordinary/critical buildup. Each accepts 0-100; 0 disables that type. The strongest applicable type wins. Maximum ordinary lineup motion.",5.0,0.0,100.0,Kind::Slider},
{"Dynamic Gameday Broadcast",L"Dynamic Gameday Broadcast",L"CriticalShakeStrengthPercent","Critical Shake Strength (%)","Random motion ceiling for qualifying close critical downs; packed house is not required. Default 10 gives 5-10%, chosen once per call. Below 5 uses the configured value; 0 disables it. Third down needs 10 or fewer yards and an offensive play; fourth down must be going for it.",10.0,0.0,100.0,Kind::Slider},
{"Dynamic Gameday Broadcast",L"Dynamic Gameday Broadcast",L"PlayReactionFadeSeconds","Play Reaction Fade Seconds","Seconds for live catch/run/turnover/return reactions to settle after the whistle: 1-8. Default 5 includes a brief hold, then a smooth fade. TDs/eruptions use separate profiles.",5.0,1.0,8.0,Kind::Choice},
{"Dynamic Gameday Broadcast",L"Dynamic Gameday Broadcast",L"PlayImpactExtraSeconds","Play Impact Extra Seconds","Extra seconds for immediately tackled catches, sacks and similar short impacts: 0-5. Default 1 gives about 6.4 seconds total with the default reaction fade. Short impacts hit quickly, hold briefly, then fade. Live runs/returns use the settling time above.",1.0,0.0,5.0,Kind::Choice},
{"Dynamic Gameday Broadcast",L"Dynamic Gameday Broadcast",L"CatchImpactShakeStrengthPercent","Catch Impact Shake Strength (%)","Separate impact strength for long catches tackled immediately: 0-30%, default 8. Applies at a dead-ball catch or when the whistle follows within 0.35 seconds. Long catches with a run afterward use the normal live-play strength instead.",8.0,0.0,30.0,Kind::Choice},
{"Dynamic Gameday Broadcast",L"Dynamic Gameday Broadcast",L"LineupCheerShakeStrengthPercent","Lineup Cheer Shake Strength (%)","Motion for a special immediate lineup cheer: 0-100%, default 5. Used inside the 10, on the first home offensive call, or the first call of a late winning drive.",5.0,0.0,100.0,Kind::Choice},
{"Dynamic Gameday Broadcast",L"Dynamic Gameday Broadcast",L"HostileOpeningShakeMaximumPercent","Hostile Opening Shake Maximum (%)","Extra movement on the game's first offensive play when the visitors start with the ball. Requires qualifying atmosphere/fullness and a home stadium; it does not repeat later. OpeningAtmosphere=0 disables this opening sequence, including its extra motion.",15.0,0.0,30.0,Kind::Choice},
{"Dynamic Gameday Broadcast",L"Dynamic Gameday Broadcast",L"TouchdownShakeStrengthPercent","Touchdown Shake Strength (%)","Sustained home-touchdown movement, or either team at a neutral site. This is the level after the opening hit; eruptions take priority.",15.0,0.0,100.0,Kind::Slider},
{"Dynamic Gameday Broadcast",L"Dynamic Gameday Broadcast",L"EruptionShakeStrengthPercent","Eruption Shake Strength (%)","Sustained eruption movement after its opening hit. Close-up cameras reduce celebration shake automatically. It does not stack with the other three types or restart during postgame carry.",22.5,0.0,100.0,Kind::Choice},
{"Dynamic Gameday Broadcast",L"Dynamic Gameday Broadcast",L"TouchdownShakeImpactPercent","Touchdown Shake Impact (%)","Opening touchdown hit: 0-100. Default 20%, then settles to the 15% level above. The opening hit lasts about a second at the default duration.",20.0,0.0,100.0,Kind::Slider},
{"Dynamic Gameday Broadcast",L"Dynamic Gameday Broadcast",L"EruptionShakeImpactPercent","Eruption Shake Impact (%)","Opening eruption hit: 0-100. Default 30%, then settles to the 22.5% level above. Each impact is at least its sustained level; setting the sustained level to 0 disables the type.",30.0,0.0,100.0,Kind::Slider},
{"Dynamic Gameday Broadcast",L"Dynamic Gameday Broadcast",L"TouchdownShakeDurationSeconds","Touchdown Shake Duration Seconds","Whole touchdown camera effect, including hold and fade: 3-30 seconds. Default 11: 20% opening hit, 15% hold through about 6 seconds, then a 5-second fade. Qualified safeties use the same strengths with 70% of this duration (7.7s by default).",11.0,3.0,30.0,Kind::Slider},
{"Dynamic Gameday Broadcast",L"Dynamic Gameday Broadcast",L"EruptionShakeDurationSeconds","Eruption Shake Duration Seconds","Whole eruption camera effect: 5-60 seconds. Default 16: 30% opening hit, 22.5% hold through about 8 seconds, then an 8-second fade. Live camera cuts and timeout scenes keep the remaining duration; zoom is compensated. A new snap, pause menu or interactive replay stops celebration shake.",16.0,5.0,60.0,Kind::Slider},
{"Dynamic Gameday Broadcast",L"Dynamic Gameday Broadcast",L"DuringPlayShakeStrengthPercent","During Play Shake Strength (%)","Motion on qualifying long catches/runs, interceptions and 30-yard kick/punt returns: 0-30%. Confirmed sacks/forced fumbles use a short impact and fade at this strength. 10 = the tested strength. The fade below follows it through the whistle; effects never stack.",10.0,0.0,30.0,Kind::Choice},
{"Logging",L"Logging",L"MaxFileMB","Max File MB","Maximum size of the main in-game log in MB: 1-16. Clears at the limit. The launcher log has its own fixed 2 MB limit. No log archives build up. Logs/status live in Plugins/DynamicGamedayAtmosphere/Logs/.",2.0,1.0,16.0,Kind::Slider},
{"Logging",L"Logging",L"Debug","Debug","0 = readable gameplay/status messages; 1 = extra technical troubleshooting detail. Leave at 0 during ordinary play.",0.0,0.0,1.0,Kind::Toggle},
